WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.057
Looking at your own CT and MRI scans, privately.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.826
What DICOM files are, why window and level matter so much, and how to view

3
00:00:09.826 --> 00:00:13.344
and share your scans without uploading medical data anywhere.

4
00:00:14.744 --> 00:00:19.565
What DICOM is. DICOM stands for Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine.

5
00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:24.407
Numbers, not colours. Here is the part that surprised me most.

6
00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:30.057
Patient data and sharing. Because DICOM files carry names, dates of birth

7
00:00:30.057 --> 00:00:34.645
and hospital details inside them, I treat them like any other medical record.

8
00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:40.374
Why do this locally. Search for an online DICOM viewer and many of the results

9
00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:42.985
upload your files to a server to process them.

10
00:00:44.285 --> 00:00:46.809
To try it, open DICOM Viewer in OpenFile.

11
00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:50.319
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

12
00:00:50.319 --> 00:00:53.459
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

13
00:00:57.385 --> 00:01:00.863
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
